Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.49,Caption,,0,0,0,,When I was training, we would keep people in traction
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.50,0:00:12.17,Caption,,0,0,0,,in the hospital for a week, just lying there
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.42,0:00:16.71,Caption,,0,0,0,,with their leg up in balanced traction, and they couldn't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.95,0:00:21.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,Those patients did just fine ultimately.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.67,0:00:25.56,Caption,,0,0,0,,Many of them got blood clots because we didn't understand the risk
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.56,0:00:30.63,Caption,,0,0,0,,of blood clots in those days, and it was a balanced
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.64,0:00:34.67,Caption,,0,0,0,,battle between preventing them from getting blood clots, yet keeping them
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.67,0:00:36.43,Caption,,0,0,0,,in bed in this balanced traction.
